    "content": "Five years of intense touring behind Lateralus transformed Danny Carey's playing and setup. The 10,000 Days recording captured an artist who had fully internalized the concepts introduced on Lateralus and was ready to push them further.\n\n**Physical Maturation:**\nFive years of 200+ night tours meant that by 2006, Danny's relationship with the SQ2 kit was completely intuitive. He no longer thought about the equipment — it had become an extension of his body. This physical mastery freed him to focus entirely on composition and expression.\n\n**Electronic First Steps:**\nThe Roland SPD-S represented Danny's first real commitment to electronic integration in Tool's studio work. Where Lateralus was almost exclusively acoustic, 10,000 Days began exploring the electronic territory that would fully blossom on Fear Inoculum. The SPD-S was relatively simple by later standards, but it established the framework for what was to come.\n\n**Compositional Complexity:**\nThe time signature work on 10,000 Days exceeded even Lateralus. \"Vicarious\" in strict 7/8, \"The Pot\" in 7/4, \"Rosetta Stoned\" cycling through 7/8, 4/4, and 9/8 — the album is a masterclass in making odd meters feel inevitable and groovy.\n\n**Gear Comparison:**",
